# rspamd FHS migration: runtime dir /run/rspamd -> /var/run/rspamd.
#
# Stale-state policy (/var/run is persistent by design, never wiped):
# - PID file: cleared at (re)start in both inits (tracked-start
#   only, never against a live daemon); the daemon rewrites it.
# - Worker/control state: recreated by the daemon on start.
# - New /var/run/rspamd: converged here on upgrade
#   (rspamd:rspamd 0755); created by tmpfiles.d (systemd) and
#   checkpath (OpenRC). The unit's old RuntimeDirectory= could only
#   create under /run and ran as the wrong owner for a persistent
#   dir, so tmpfiles.d replaces it (mariadb precedent).
# - Old /run/rspamd: volatile residue on tmpfs. Removed once empty;
#   left in place and reported while the old daemon runs.

dir /var/run/rspamd 0755 rspamd rspamd
rmdir-if-empty /run/rspamd
